From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 14:57:46 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Watch world threads, and keep a world's failure to that world

A watchdog checks the world threads once a second: one that has gone
worldThreadStallSeconds (athena.yml, 10) without finishing a tick is logged with
its stack and reported by WorldThreadStallEvent, and again once it ticks again;
the server and the other worlds go on. A throwable out of a world's tick stops
only that thread: the server thread takes the world back halted (owned, no longer
ticked), calls WorldThreadFailureEvent and sends the players still in it to the
main world's spawn. Scoreboards' list and the scores vanilla keeps by criteria
(deaths, kills, health) are updated under one lock; masks, disguises and boss
bars check the thread of the player's world, and a disguise re-registers the
player for each viewer on that viewer's thread; players are saved on the thread
of their world; the index audit runs on the server thread only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

